(3) Provision of a defense against the claim or proceeding would not be in the best interests of the City of Fairburn, Georgia;
(4) The proceeding is a criminal prosecution; provided, however, that a defense shall not be refused where the criminal prosecution is one for an alleged violation of the Georgia Open Records Act or Georgia Open Meetings Act, and it is determined that the charged employee, officer, or elected official has acted in good faith to comply with the subject Act and has substantially complied with all city policies relating to the subject Act, which determination shall be made by city council;
(5) The request was not timely or properly made, after the happening of an event that possibly gives rise to a claim for indemnification under this division;
(6) The claim arises out of an act or omission at a time when the covered individual was under the influence of unlawful drugs, alcohol or other intoxicants;
(7) The act or omission giving rise to the claim was in direct disobedience of a lawful order or instruction by a superior (or such other lawful directive) or in contravention of approved city policy;
(8) The failure to cooperate in the defense of a claim or proceeding arising following the effective date of this division;
(9) Following approval, it is determined that one or more of the grounds for refusal set forth in this section exist;
(10) The conduct resulted in a finding and determination by the ethics board that a violation of the ethics code occurred, which shall disqualify the public official from city-funded defense or indemnification. In the event the charged official is acquitted or the charges are dismissed, the reimbursement provision in the ethics code shall be the only source for which reimbursement can be sought and not this division; or
(11) The claim arises or relates to an act or omission that precedes the effective date of the ordinance from which this division is derived.
(b) The determinations required by this section shall be made by [the] mayor and council as provided herein.
